  "2026-10-21T19:36:26.184Z",codex-agent,"Authorized tracker reconciliation, audit 2026-10-21. Owner-authorized takeover of any historical assignment for this verified terminal transition. Reverified current main 4db41b03f85f: merged #24 (b479dd0); owner no-Git contract of 2026-10-20 still supersedes this Git-only work; source tree exactly matches the audited snapshot. **PR 24 immutable history integration needs an approved merge procedure.** [PR #24](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-jev/pull/24) is already merged (b479dd0). The requested Git-specific immutable-history merge procedure is superseded by the 2026-10-20 prohibition on merge-driver/receipt work."
  "2026-10-22T11:14:52.527Z",codex-agent,"PR 39 review: PRRT_kwDOU8IMzs6vKEU8 is valid. Main still contains four previously re-anchored events; the no-Git contract does not waive immutable history. Reopening this finding by appended tracker updates, without rewriting existing events. All review threads/comments and latest CodeRabbit body fetched completely; no Outside diff range findings. Main merged while retaining the existing divergent PR history stream; the default pinned merge driver attempted union_reanchor and was aborted before commit. Original main-side event remains available in the main parent; its current metadata will be appended using the pinned CLI instead of re-hashing that event. Full tracker-only diff checked for similar unsupported terminal transitions."
  "2026-10-22T11:18:35.255Z",codex-agent,"PR 39 evidence: linked regression passes 1/1, verifying status open and all 34 original cad06f4 history prefixes by length plus SHA-256. The same status assertion against git show cad06f4:.agents/pm/issues/pm-jev-i3wg.toon fails with exit 1 because the original record is canceled (tracker evidence revert proof). The four inherited re-anchored records remain unchanged; this fixes the false cancellation, not the pre-existing integrity defect. npm ci passed with zero vulnerabilities; changelog generation/check and git diff --check passed. Fresh no-local clone with isolated identity and installed merge drivers passes strict pm health: 10 checks, zero failing, one stale-item advisory. Package worktree health exits 0 but reports existing extension SDK skew and an orphaned receipt from the aborted merge; one required reconcile attempt refused no_receipt_set_proves_snapshot with no history changes. No force repair attempted. Other terminal transitions were checked against main and merged delivery evidence; no additional valid findings. Releasing claim; keep item open. PM limitation: pinned default merge driver proposes union_reanchor on divergent history; pm claim requires reopening terminal items before claiming."
